# spline_cap_rough.cam — scallop-mode stock_to_leave roughing on the analytic
# spline cap (DECISIONS.md "stock_to_leave mixed meridians…").
# spline_cap_scallop.cam's freeform meridian run as a ROUGHING pass, and the
# one carrier whose meridian is USER-AUTHORED: the march's osculating triangle
# (curvature picked per march point, inflated to R ± a' by pointwise sign) is
# only the SPACING heuristic here — across-step curvature drift on a freeform
# curve can push a pair's true cusp past the scallop, so the budget is the
# EXACT cusp-tip walk over the march's own emitted grid (sweep-then-VERIFY,
# the cone/ogive scheme), with the nominal distance under each tip read by
# bounded numeric projection (dense per-knot-span seed + Newton polish — the
# residual argument that separates the spline from the Mesh error).
#
# The 0.5mm allowance is a ceiling on TOTAL remaining material including this
# pass's own cusps (max, not min): the verified budget is 0.205mm — the 0.2
# scallop target plus the drift the triangle couldn't see, exactly the number
# that would silently breach the ceiling if the scallop were trusted by fiat —
# leaving nominal skin a' = 0.295mm. Hand-checked anchor: the meridian's apex
# tangent is (3, −1)/√10 (control polygon (0,20)→(3,19)), so the first CL
# point rides the tilted apex normal at r_ball + a' = 3.295:
# (3.295/√10, 20 + 3·3.295/√10) = (1.042, 23.126) → X51.042, Z23.126.
#
# CONTAINED 2026-08-13 (DECISIONS.md "rim-area accounting…", slice 2):
# the stock used to stop AT this feature's base plane, so the whole
# surface stood in air and the fixture only ran because there was
# nothing to hit. The stock now stands 2mm proud of the feature's top
# (z 22) and T1 roughs the moat before the finish;
# numbers in the older comments describe the same toolpath, whose
# motion is unchanged where it touches the surface.
units mm
feed 600
plunge 200
rapid_z 25
clearance_z 40
spindle 4000

stock Box(w=100, l=80, h=62, x=0, y=0, z=22)

tool T1 Endmill(dia=12.0)
tool T10 Ballmill(dia=6.0)

# The freeform cubic b-spline meridian (see meridian.spline): apex on the
# axis at z=20, base rim at r=13, z=0 — convex toward the tool everywhere.
feature Cap SplineRevolve(file="meridian.spline", x=50, y=40, z=0)

run Clear(tool=T1, profile=Cap, stepover=8.0, stepdown=5.0, stock_to_leave=1)
run Copy(tool=T10, surface=Cap, scallop=0.2, stock_to_leave=0.5)
